# Display refresh

Every on-screen motion is one frame of the window's monitor. Never faster, and never a fixed 60 Hz on a faster panel.

- Slint `animate` is already vsync'd. Do not add a second timer to "smooth" it.
- Custom visual loops (window zoom, page settle, video frame pump) use `crate::platform::frame_interval()` (or `frame_interval_from_hz` when you already have the screen). No `from_millis(4)` / `from_millis(8)` animation ticks.
- Trackpad scrolling applies each AppKit delta as it arrives. Do not start a Slint coast on top of macOS momentum.
- Progress bars, debug stats, and other non-motion polls may run slower than the display. They must not run faster.

```rust
// BAD — outruns a 120 Hz panel and jitters on 60 Hz
timer.start(TimerMode::Repeated, Duration::from_millis(4), step);

// GOOD
timer.start(TimerMode::Repeated, crate::platform::frame_interval(), step);
```

CI: `sh scripts/lint-display-refresh.sh` fails Repeated timers with `Duration::from_millis(N)` when `N ≤ 16`.
